哦，她有没有说，好吧，你嫁给我吧？

00:44:04.219 --> 00:44:05.219
She said, well, you marry me.
她说，好吧，你嫁给我吧。

00:44:05.219 --> 00:44:06.219
Yeah.
是的。

00:44:06.219 --> 00:44:07.219
That's what I got to propose.
这就是我要提议的。

00:44:07.219 --> 00:44:08.219
So that's a good.
所以这是一件好事。

00:44:08.219 --> 00:44:13.820
If for those young actors out there, yes, if you audition and you got to propose you with the guest manager, you're probably going to get that right.
如果对于那些年轻演员来说，是的，如果你试镜并且你必须向客座经理推荐你，你可能会做对的。

00:44:13.820 --> 00:44:14.820
Yeah.
是的。

00:44:14.820 --> 00:44:15.820
You call your agent afterwards.
之后你打电话给你的经纪人。

00:44:15.820 --> 00:44:16.820
You say, well, I did this whole speech.
你说，好吧，整个演讲都是我做的。

00:44:16.820 --> 00:44:18.820
And afterwards, the cast director said, will you marry me?
然后演员导演说，你愿意嫁给我吗？

00:44:18.820 --> 00:44:19.820
Do you think that's a good sign?
你认为这是一个好兆头吗？

00:44:19.820 --> 00:44:22.739
Oh, so we all wanted to marry you.
哦，所以我们都想嫁给你。

00:44:22.739 --> 00:44:23.820
We all felt that way.
我们都有这样的感觉。

00:44:23.820 --> 00:44:25.340
We were you melted our hearts.
我们是你融化了我们的心。

00:44:25.340 --> 00:44:28.539
So I remember going back to my car.
所以我记得回到我的车里。

00:44:28.539 --> 00:44:41.500
And so this is very inside baseball, and I don't even know if it's still this way, but you used to have to test for the studio and test for the network theory, these two hoops, if you got past the initial producer session, which is what I had with you guys.
所以这是棒球内部的事情，我什至不知道是否仍然如此，但是如果你通过了最初的制作人会议，这就是我和你们一起进行的，那么你过去必须测试工作室并测试网络理论，这两个圈子。

00:44:41.500 --> 00:44:47.059
So I, oh, also this is maybe worth mentioning.
所以我，哦，这也许也值得一提。

00:44:47.059 --> 00:44:58.019
My agent at the time, who I was with for about 14 years, she used to tell me the only power you have as a young actor is the ability to say no, and I didn't have much power.
我当时的经纪人，和我在一起大约 14 年，她经常告诉我，作为一名年轻演员，你唯一的权力就是拒绝的能力，而我没有太多权力。

00:44:58.019 --> 00:45:00.059
I didn't, I wasn't a known actor.
我没有，我不是一个知名演员。

00:45:00.059 --> 00:45:04.820
I was known in the business, cast New Actors New Me, a couple of showrunners New Me.
我在业内很出名，演员阵容包括新演员新我、几位节目主持人新我。

00:45:04.820 --> 00:45:10.099
But I had gotten a reputation as being like a little picky as a young actor.
但作为一名年轻演员，我被认为有点挑剔。

00:45:10.099 --> 00:45:11.980
And I remember Megan had pitched.
我记得梅根已经投过球了。

00:45:11.980 --> 00:45:13.179
We were told that by Megan.
梅根告诉我们这一点。

00:45:13.179 --> 00:45:14.179
Yeah, Megan had pitched.
是的，梅根已经投球了。

00:45:14.179 --> 00:45:15.820
I really wanted to tell that.
我真的很想告诉你这一点。

00:45:15.820 --> 00:45:16.900
I don't know if he'll come in.
我不知道他是否会进来。

00:45:16.900 --> 00:45:17.940
He's picky.
他很挑剔。

00:45:17.940 --> 00:45:22.500
So when you saw me on the list, you're like, oh, Josh Radder's going to like you.
所以当你在名单上看到我时，你会想，哦，乔什·雷德会喜欢你的。

00:45:22.500 --> 00:45:23.739
So we felt accepted by you.
所以我们感觉被你接受了。

00:45:23.739 --> 00:45:25.059
We were like, he liked us.
我们就像，他喜欢我们。

00:45:25.059 --> 00:45:26.380
The picky guy liked us.
那个挑剔的家伙喜欢我们。

00:45:26.380 --> 00:45:27.420
Yeah, yeah.
是啊是啊。

00:45:27.420 --> 00:45:28.260
We were so needy.
我们是如此需要帮助。

00:45:28.260 --> 00:45:32.659
So that was a real gift my agent gave me was saying like, be discerning, you know?
所以这是我的经纪人给我的一份真正的礼物，就像是说，要有洞察力，你知道吗？

00:45:32.659 --> 00:45:36.780
So I would only throw my hat in the rings for stuff I really believed in.
所以我只会为我真正相信的事情而奋斗。

00:45:36.780 --> 00:45:38.659
And I believed in your show.
我相信你的表演。

00:45:38.659 --> 00:45:43.219
By the time I got back to the car, my agent called me and she said, well, that was quick.
当我回到车上时，我的经纪人打电话给我，她说，好吧，那很快。

00:45:43.219 --> 00:45:45.219
They want to do a test deal with you.
他们想与你进行测试交易。

00:45:45.219 --> 00:45:46.739
They want to take you to the studio.
他们想带你去工作室。

00:45:46.739 --> 00:45:48.099
Your car was 10 feet away.
你的车在 10 英尺外。

00:45:48.099 --> 00:45:54.210
So then you guys also had a couple more days of seeing other Ted's, right?
那么你们还有几天时间去见其他特德，对吧？

00:45:54.210 --> 00:46:03.969
We had to keep seeing other Ted's even though we knew It's so shitty, I feel bad, because we knew we had you, and then other people come in, and nobody could be you.
我们不得不继续见到其他特德，尽管我们知道这太糟糕了，我感觉很糟糕，因为我们知道我们拥有你，然后其他人进来，没有人可以成为你。

00:46:03.969 --> 00:46:19.969
Great actors, great people came in, and you need to go into the studio with a few, and network to test, to go into a room with the executives and have you, and as it turned out, Kobe, do chemistry reads and see, we had to have that happen with a couple of other people, but we knew we were in love with you.
伟大的演员，伟大的人进来了，你需要和一些人一起进入工作室，并进行网络测试，进入一个与高管一起的房间并拥有你，结果是，科比，做化学阅读并看看，我们必须与其他几个人一起发生这种情况，但我们知道我们爱上了你。

00:46:19.969 --> 00:46:25.992
All of us were, and that's harrowing, because we could have had a different feeling the network.
我们所有人都是如此，这令人痛苦，因为我们可能会对网络有不同的感觉。

00:46:25.992 --> 00:46:29.191
The network could have been like, no, it's not him.
网络可能会说，不，不是他。

00:46:29.191 --> 00:46:31.826
And that would have been so heartbreaking.
那真是令人心碎。

00:46:31.826 --> 00:46:35.276
But everybody you went after the other went, we get it.
但每个人都追随另一个人，我们明白了。

00:46:35.276 --> 00:46:37.221
And that doesn't always happen.
但这并不总是发生。

00:46:37.221 --> 00:46:39.793
Either kids, that does not always happen.
无论是孩子，这并不总是发生。

00:46:39.793 --> 00:46:40.293
Yeah.
是的。

00:46:40.293 --> 00:46:45.687
Well, I've found in in show business, and maybe it's like this in other areas of life.
嗯，我在演艺界发现了这一点，也许生活的其他领域也是如此。

00:46:45.687 --> 00:46:48.636
But if a job is not yours, the door won't open.
但如果工作不是你的，门就不会打开。

00:46:49.170 --> 00:46:50.634
It just simply won't open.
它只是打不开。

00:46:50.634 --> 00:47:06.121
No matter how right you think you are for it, how much you want it, If the job is yours, the doors keep flying open and I've learned to trust effortlessness in my career, like when you click with people and it's easy and fun and you're all just the enthusiasm is really high.
无论你认为自己有多正确，你有多想要它，如果这份工作是你的，大门就会一直敞开，我学会了相信我的职业生涯毫不费力，就像当你与人相处时，这很容易、很有趣，而且你们都热情很高。

00:47:06.121 --> 00:47:07.698
You want to make this thing.
你想做这个东西。

00:47:07.698 --> 00:47:12.598
I don't, I sometimes think effort, like hard grinding effort can be a little overrated.
我不这么认为，我有时认为努力，比如艰苦的努力可能有点被高估了。

00:47:12.598 --> 00:47:16.428
That you need to pay attention to where things are actually in flow.
你需要注意事情实际上在哪里进行。

00:47:16.428 --> 00:47:17.385
Yeah, absolutely.
是的，绝对是。

00:47:17.385 --> 00:47:31.746
And that's cool to hear you say that because I, you know, from the, and you've now been on both sides of the table, having, having written and directed your own movies and stuff, like, it is like you, at the beginning of these sessions, you get this list.
听到你这么说真是太酷了，因为我，你知道，从那时开始，你现在已经站在了谈判桌的两边，编写和导演了自己的电影和东西，就像你一样，在这些会议开始时，你得到了这个清单。

00:47:31.746 --> 00:47:34.506
And, you know, and here's who we're seeing today.
而且，你知道，这就是我们今天看到的人。

00:47:34.506 --> 00:47:39.969
And it's like a list and it's like a name and then a little space for you to write your comments.
它就像一个列表，就像一个名字，然后是一个供您写评论的小空间。

00:47:39.969 --> 00:47:43.967
And so it's just like a very clean sheet of paper with like nine names.
所以它就像一张非常干净的纸，上面有九个名字。

00:47:43.967 --> 00:47:56.019
And you just like see that And you think like these are like nine people right now just hoping that that they're like and it's by the way, it's this like nine different branches of like where the universe could go.
你只是喜欢看到这一点 你认为这些就像现在的九个人只是希望他们就像，顺便说一句，这就像宇宙可以去的九个不同的分支。

00:47:56.019 --> 00:48:02.900
This could be a show with this person as Ted and this person as Ted and it's it's yeah.
这可能是一个节目，这个人是特德，这个人是特德，是的。

00:48:02.900 --> 00:48:12.860
And I feel like there's it's a lot of the stuff we talked about on how many your mother because just the fact that like Destiny so it takes such a big part in in the search for love.
我觉得我们谈论了很多关于你母亲的事情，因为就像《命运》一样，它在寻找爱的过程中扮演了如此重要的角色。

00:48:12.860 --> 00:48:20.675
you know, I feel like how I met your mother at its core is like, it's this struggle between is falling in love something that I go out and seek.
你知道，我觉得我遇见你母亲的本质就像是，这种斗争就是坠入爱河，我出去寻找。

00:48:20.675 --> 00:48:24.691
Do I take action to meet the person that I spend the rest of my life with?
我是否会采取行动去见那个与我共度余生的人？

00:48:24.691 --> 00:48:26.753
Or is it something that happens to me?
或者是发生在我身上的事情？

00:48:26.753 --> 00:48:29.033
I have to just sit back and let it happen.
我必须坐下来让它发生。

00:48:29.033 --> 00:48:31.421
And that's like, that's the casting process.
这就是选角过程。

00:48:31.421 --> 00:48:35.980
I mean, it really is like, I feel like there's no way to, there's no answer to that.
我的意思是，这真的是，我觉得没有办法，没有答案。

00:48:35.980 --> 00:48:37.500
It's an unsolvable question.
这是一个无解的问题。

00:48:37.500 --> 00:48:38.354
There's a good theme.
有一个很好的主题。

00:48:38.354 --> 00:48:44.780
A good theme has emerged of our conversation of just like, there's some preparation and then there's some luck in letting you and leading it to that part too.
我们的谈话出现了一个很好的主题，就像，有一些准备，然后有一些运气让你也把它带到那部分。

00:48:44.780 --> 00:48:50.659
And your reaction writing too, it's like you can't, if you're forcing it too hard, that might be a sign and it's not quite right.
你的反应也是如此，就像你不能，如果你强迫得太用力，这可能是一个迹象，而且不太正确。

00:48:50.659 --> 00:48:52.699
And the doors did keep opening for you.
大门确实一直为你敞开。

00:48:52.699 --> 00:48:59.900
In some ways, you guys had to honor the themes of your show and the creation of your show.
在某些方面，你们必须尊重节目的主题和节目的创作。

00:48:59.900 --> 00:49:00.900
Yeah.
是的。

00:49:00.900 --> 00:49:01.900
Do you know what I'm saying?
你知道我在说什么吗？

00:49:01.900 --> 00:49:06.659
Like, you had to be open to like the right person at the right time.
就像，你必须开放地在正确的时间喜欢正确的人。

00:49:06.659 --> 00:49:07.659
Yeah.
是的。

00:49:07.659 --> 00:49:08.659
So I'm trying to remember.
所以我努力回忆。

00:49:08.659 --> 00:49:12.739
I go to the studio, you had one other guy there.
我去了工作室，那里还有另外一个人。

00:49:12.739 --> 00:49:13.739
I think another 10.
我想还有10个。

00:49:13.739 --> 00:49:15.019
Yeah, the other guy was who we say it was.
是的，另一个人就是我们所说的那个人。

00:49:15.019 --> 00:49:16.460
We can say it was it was Bob Sagitt.
我们可以说是鲍勃·萨吉特。

00:49:16.460 --> 00:49:19.420
He was a little too old for the role and that's why he became a future 10.
他对于这个角色来说有点太老了，这就是他成为未来十号的原因。

00:49:19.420 --> 00:49:21.820
A consolation prize.
安慰奖。

00:49:21.820 --> 00:49:25.420
Yeah, it was, he was really good, but it's like, here's a little old.
是的，他确实很棒，但感觉有点老了。

00:49:25.420 --> 00:49:27.420
But now, now I know.
但现在，现在我知道了。

00:49:27.420 --> 00:49:28.900
I don't think we should say names of who it would be.
我认为我们不应该说出是谁的名字。

00:49:28.900 --> 00:49:30.059
No, no, no, that's not what I was saying.
不不不，我不是这个意思。

00:49:30.059 --> 00:49:31.300
And everything was just lies.
而一切都只是谎言。

00:49:31.300 --> 00:49:33.300
But very talented, another very tough guy.
但非常有才华，也是一个非常硬朗的人。

00:49:33.300 --> 00:49:34.940
You know, I'm just gonna, can I just throw this in?
你知道，我只是想，我可以把这个扔进去吗？

00:49:34.940 --> 00:49:36.380
It's someone, I remember being there.
是一个人，我记得在那儿。

00:49:36.380 --> 00:49:51.940
And because you go to these things, and there's two, there's always two, and everyone in the room, including the head executives at CBS, everybody knows, there's the guy that they want, and then there's the other guy that they're bringing in, just to show like, yeah, but we really want this guy.
因为你去这些事情，有两个，总是有两个，房间里的每个人，包括哥伦比亚广播公司的首席执行官，每个人都知道，他们想要一个人，然后他们引进另一个人，只是为了表明，是的，但我们真的想要这个人。

00:49:51.940 --> 00:49:55.460
And I think everyone knew that, including both of the actors involved.
我想每个人都知道这一点，包括涉及的两位演员。

00:49:55.460 --> 00:50:03.340
And I remember feeling just because my mind always says, like how can I have more anxiety about this moment?
我记得这种感觉只是因为我的大脑总是在说，我怎样才能对这一刻感到更加焦虑？

00:50:03.340 --> 00:50:05.300
Okay, I'll feel bad for this guy.
好吧，我会为这个人感到难过。

00:50:05.300 --> 00:50:12.460
And I remember because he was really, and I'm not to say who he was, but he went on to be super funny and great on another show.
我记得因为他确实是，我不是说他是谁，但他在另一场节目中表现得非常有趣和出色。

00:50:12.460 --> 00:50:14.619
That was, that I was a huge fan on it.
也就是说，我是它的超级粉丝。

00:50:14.619 --> 00:50:18.420
And so it was, it was, it worked out right.
事情就是这样，事情确实如此，结果是正确的。

00:50:18.420 --> 00:50:19.260
It was nice to see that.
很高兴看到这一点。

00:50:19.260 --> 00:50:23.219
Can I say the, I do know this story that really made me laugh.
我可以说，我确实知道这个让我发笑的故事。

00:50:23.219 --> 00:50:27.139
It's a Rob Greenberg line because I think I also had to read a Barney scene.
这是罗布·格林伯格的台词，因为我想我还必须读一下巴尼的场景。

00:50:27.139 --> 00:50:32.539
It was, it was Barney trying to get me to go to laser tag or something in the test.
是的，巴尼试图让我参加激光枪战或其他测试。

00:50:32.539 --> 00:50:41.179
and Rob Greenberg apparently said afterwards about the other guy, I feel like he wants to go to laser tag, like he would go to laser tag.
罗布·格林伯格后来显然谈到了另一个人，我觉得他想去激光枪战，就像他会去激光枪战一样。

00:50:41.179 --> 00:50:44.300
I really think Josh did not want to go to laser tag with this guy.
我真的认为乔什不想和这个家伙一起去激光枪战。

00:50:44.300 --> 00:50:48.940
Yeah, yeah, yeah, really a little jockier, a little different energy.
是啊，是啊，是啊，真的有点兴奋，有点不同的能量。

00:50:48.940 --> 00:50:52.059
Yeah, yeah, yeah, it had to be plausible that you would not have gone.
是啊，是啊，是啊，你不会走一定是有道理的。

00:50:52.059 --> 00:50:54.219
And you would not have gone to laser tag and that's why you were right.
你不会去激光标记，这就是为什么你是对的。

00:50:54.219 --> 00:51:10.924
No, I'm just curious, like, just when people become so important and kind of iconic in your life, like there's that moment when you, when you see them for the first time that kind of gets etched in in your own personal history, like I'm just curious what, how you envisioned Robyn Sherbatsky.
不，我只是好奇，就像，当人们在你的生活中变得如此重要和具有标志性时，就像你第一次看到他们的那一刻，那种感觉被铭刻在你自己的个人历史中，就像我只是好奇你是如何想象罗宾·谢尔巴茨基的。

00:51:10.924 --> 00:51:14.356
I don't know if that was her last name in the pilot, was it?
我不知道这是否是她在飞行员中的姓氏，是吗？

00:51:14.356 --> 00:51:16.473
I think you came up with that letter.
我想那封信是你想出来的。

00:51:16.473 --> 00:51:22.308
Yeah, it's, it was, it was a Sherb, Robyn Kitty Sherbatsky is a character from Anna Karenina, I think.
是的，它是，它是，它是一个 Sherb，我认为 Robyn Kitty Sherbatsky 是《安娜·卡列尼娜》中的角色。

00:51:22.308 --> 00:51:31.289
I like, I think I was like, thought I'd, I mean, I painted myself a reader and And I was like, I'm going to read Anna Karenina and got like 20 pages into it.
我喜欢，我想我想，我想，我的意思是，我把自己画成一个读者，我想，我要读《安娜·卡列尼娜》，读了大约 20 页。

00:51:31.289 --> 00:51:36.369
And then, yeah, yeah, exactly.
然后，是的，是的，完全正确。

00:51:36.369 --> 00:51:39.849
So you told Stoy, I got you.
所以你告诉斯托伊，我抓住你了。

00:51:39.849 --> 00:51:45.340
Did you have an idea in your head of who this woman was?
你心里知道这个女人是谁吗？

00:51:45.340 --> 00:51:48.940
It's interesting because you've got five main characters.
这很有趣，因为你有五个主角。

00:51:48.940 --> 00:51:52.420
Four of them were absolutely drawn from real life.
其中四个绝对取材于现实生活。

00:51:52.420 --> 00:52:03.900
Like Ted Marshall and Lily were me, Craig and Rebecca, you know, and again, like, then then it becomes some kind of the writers come in and like add their own hang their own stuff on the Christmas tree.
就像特德·马歇尔和莉莉是我一样，克雷格和丽贝卡，你知道，然后又变成了某种作家进来，喜欢在圣诞树上添加他们自己的东西。

00:52:03.900 --> 00:52:13.900
But and Barney was very much inspired by a couple guys that sort of wore that kind of false staffian presence in our lives when we lived in New York.
但是，当我们住在纽约时，巴尼受到了一些人的启发，他们在我们的生活中扮演着一种假职员的角色。

00:52:13.900 --> 00:52:18.739
The only character who was completely made up whole cloth was Robin.
唯一一个完全由整块布组成的角色是罗宾。

00:52:18.739 --> 00:52:26.739
And so it really was like the casting process was sort of this process of like, let's see if we can find her.
所以选角过程真的就像是这样的过程，让我们看看是否能找到她。

00:52:26.739 --> 00:52:27.739
Let's see who this could be.
让我们看看这可能是谁。

00:52:27.739 --> 00:52:44.659
It really was like, it wasn't like, oh yeah, I mean, I haven't noticed like, I think Neil got cast as Barney despite the fact that he sort of was physically nothing like the, the, the people that Barney was, was based on, but like that, you know, I remember you guys talking around Jack Black as a prototype.
这真的就像，哦，是的，我的意思是，我没有注意到，我认为尼尔被选为巴尼，尽管事实上他的身体状况与巴尼的原型完全不同，但就像那样，你知道，我记得你们谈论杰克·布莱克作为原型。

00:52:44.659 --> 00:52:59.500
Like yeah, I think you saw him much more like a fast road that was bigger and yeah, yeah, there was, there was like a Vince Vaughn road and like a Jack Black road, but we were more down the Jack Black road, I think that wouldn't you say Carter and then like, you know, came and it was like, shit, that's too good.
是的，我想你看到他更像是一条更大的快速道路，是的，是的，有，就像文斯·沃恩路和杰克·布莱克路，但我们更多的是沿着杰克·布莱克路，我想你不会说卡特，然后就像，你知道，来了，就像，妈的，那太好了。

00:52:59.500 --> 00:53:00.500
It's too good.
太好了。

00:53:00.500 --> 00:53:15.420
But I do think the one insight that I think we happened upon that I'm proud of us for happening upon was this feeling because of course you get picked up and of course the first thing is like, who can we get in it that will help its chances of getting on the air?
但我确实认为，我认为我们偶然发现的一个让我感到自豪的洞察力就是这种感觉，因为当然你会被接住，当然第一件事就是，我们可以让谁加入来帮助它有机会播出？

00:53:15.420 --> 00:53:16.260
Who's famous?
谁有名？

00:53:16.260 --> 00:53:26.650
But there was a feeling like I remember thinking like so much of Robin is built into this moment where Ted looks across the crowded bar and sees this person.
但我记得有一种感觉，就像罗宾的大部分内容都融入到了泰德穿过拥挤的酒吧并看到这个人的那一刻。

00:53:26.650 --> 00:53:30.050
and we see her for the first time as Ted Singer for the first time.
我们第一次看到她以泰德·辛格的身份出现。

00:53:30.050 --> 00:53:35.090
And if it's someone that you already have this built-in expectation of, like, oh, I loved her in this, right?
如果你已经对这个人有这种内在的期望，比如，哦，我爱她，对吧？

00:53:35.090 --> 00:53:36.250
I hate her in that.
我讨厌她这一点。

00:53:36.250 --> 00:53:41.050
Like, you're already, you're outside of the moment, and you're not having that.
就像，你已经在这一刻之外了，而你却没有那样的感觉。

00:53:41.050 --> 00:53:45.250
It's not that moment of like, there's a mystery here to be solved.
这不是那个时刻，这里有一个谜团需要解开。

00:53:45.250 --> 00:53:47.170
I want to get to know this person.
我想认识这个人。

00:53:47.170 --> 00:53:51.650
But it can't be like, you see, you see a person and you're like, I know what you did last summer.
但它不能像，你看，你看到一个人，你就像，我知道你去年夏天做了什么。

00:53:51.650 --> 00:53:52.650
It can't be.
不可能。

00:53:52.650 --> 00:53:56.063
It has to be like, I have to know what they did last summer.
就像，我必须知道他们去年夏天做了什么。

00:53:56.063 --> 00:54:00.614
You have to not know what they did any summer because tell me about your summer.
你不必知道他们每个夏天都做了什么，因为请告诉我你的夏天。

00:54:00.614 --> 00:54:06.360
I think a mystery about me and Kobe's relative obscurity or anonymity at that point really served us.
我认为关于我和科比当时相对默默无闻或匿名的神秘感确实对我们很有帮助。

00:54:06.360 --> 00:54:12.505
It served you guys in the story because you're, for sure, discovering these people, you're discovering them.
它对故事中的你们很有帮助，因为你们肯定正在发现这些人，你们正在发现他们。

00:54:12.505 --> 00:54:19.901
And you want to feel like you, you've just happened upon them rather than having any, you know, sort of foreign knowledge of them.
你想要感觉自己只是偶然发现了它们，而不是对它们有任何外国知识。

00:54:19.901 --> 00:54:25.135
Yeah, it was perfect who was more famous than who was not more famous in that of those five.
是的，这五个人中谁更有名，谁比谁不更有名，这是完美的。

00:54:25.135 --> 00:54:26.330
You know what I mean?
你知道我的意思？

00:54:26.329 --> 00:54:30.615
Like the perfect, the famous people fell into the right spots in the cast.
就像完美的人一样，名人在演员阵容中也处于正确的位置。

00:54:30.615 --> 00:54:31.484
And we met you.
我们遇见了你。

00:54:31.484 --> 00:54:33.163
The word met is in the title.
标题中有遇见这个词。

00:54:33.163 --> 00:54:34.669
It's about meeting people.
这是关于与人见面。

00:54:34.669 --> 00:54:35.364
We meet Ted.
我们见到了特德。

00:54:35.364 --> 00:54:37.564
We never, we've never seen you before.
我们从来没有见过你。

00:54:37.564 --> 00:54:38.375
We meet Robin.
我们遇见了罗宾。

00:54:38.375 --> 00:54:39.649
And that you're right.
你是对的。

00:54:39.649 --> 00:54:41.849
It was like the audience met you guys.
就像观众认识了你们一样。

00:54:41.849 --> 00:54:49.769
But Carter, it also occurs to me when you're, when you're talking about Robin being invented out of whole cloth on some level, she was the woman you were hoping to meet, right?
但是卡特，当你谈论罗宾在某种程度上被完全创造出来时，我也想到了，她就是你希望见到的女人，对吧？

00:54:49.769 --> 00:55:01.489
Like she was, you know, she became dimensional and spiky and all these things, but she was like, what if I looked across the bar and just spotted this woman?
就像她一样，你知道，她变得立体、尖锐等等，但她就像，如果我望向酒吧对面，刚刚发现这个女人怎么办？

00:55:01.489 --> 00:55:02.489
What would she be?
她会是什么样子？

00:55:02.489 --> 00:55:03.489
For sure.
一定。

00:55:03.489 --> 00:55:04.489
Yeah.
是的。

00:55:04.489 --> 00:55:05.489
She was built that way.
她就是这样建造的。

00:55:05.489 --> 00:55:12.170
It was a combination of like, make her everything that would be like, of course, he falls in love with this person.
这是一种喜欢的结合，让她的一切都会像，当然，他爱上了这个人。

00:55:12.170 --> 00:55:38.064
also give her things that it was almost like it's in sort of like judoing the like what's the tension of this series going to be like we've got this character this who just wants to you know his drive is fallen love he's like has this like he gets hit my lightning in this first episode of like Eureka I want to get married I'm like ready okay my friend just got engaged.
也给她一些东西，就像柔道一样，这个系列的紧张感是什么，我们有这个角色，他只是想让你知道他的动力是坠入爱河，他就像在《尤里卡》的第一集中被闪电击中，我想结婚，我准备好了，我的朋友刚刚订婚了。

00:55:38.064 --> 00:55:39.600
I want to settle down.
我想安定下来。

00:55:39.600 --> 00:55:41.764
Like, how do we create tension?
比如，我们如何制造紧张感？

00:55:41.764 --> 00:55:53.489
And I feel like that sort of like naturally led to Robin just becoming this character that her central drive, at least at the beginning, is I don't want to settle that.
我觉得这种感觉很自然地导致罗宾成为这个角色，她的核心驱动力，至少在一开始，是我不想解决这个问题。

00:55:53.489 --> 00:56:00.801
But I do remember by first seeing Kobe for the first time, down a hallway, walking towards me.
但我确实记得第一次见到科比，是在走廊里，向我走来。

00:56:00.801 --> 00:56:05.857
And, you know, you just have to do all this, you know, chit chat.
而且，你知道，你只需要做这一切，你知道，闲聊。

00:56:05.857 --> 00:56:11.224
And then you are supposed to, you know, simulate this thing together.
然后你们应该一起模拟这个东西。

00:56:11.224 --> 00:56:14.880
But I do remember at, I think the network test.
但我确实记得，我认为是网络测试。

00:56:14.880 --> 00:56:18.250
So it was just me by the time, I think you, you just brought me to the network.
所以当时只有我一个人，我想是你，你刚刚把我带到了网络上。

00:56:18.250 --> 00:56:18.847
Is that right?
是这样吗？

00:56:18.847 --> 00:56:20.000
Or did you bring both guys?
还是两个人都带了？

00:56:20.000 --> 00:56:21.323
God, Carter, do you remember?
天哪，卡特，你还记得吗？

00:56:21.323 --> 00:56:24.199
I feel like in the network, you have to still bring two people.
我感觉在网络里，还是得带两个人。

00:56:24.199 --> 00:56:27.188
I feel like it's always, there's always another person I can't remember.
我总觉得，总有一个我记不起的人。

00:56:27.188 --> 00:56:28.599
But maybe to see you by the point.
但也许是为了顺便见你。

00:56:28.599 --> 00:56:34.159
Because when you were with Kobe in a scene, that was the network, I think, and that was probably just you guys.
因为当你和科比一起出现在一个场景中时，我认为那就是网络，而那可能只是你们。

00:56:34.159 --> 00:56:35.159
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

00:56:35.159 --> 00:56:36.159
That was okay.
没关系。

00:56:36.159 --> 00:56:37.159
So maybe the studio is a big deal.
所以也许工作室很重要。

00:56:37.159 --> 00:56:39.320
That's the last step before you were officially hired.
这是您被正式聘用之前的最后一步。

00:56:39.320 --> 00:56:40.320
Yeah.
是的。

00:56:40.320 --> 00:57:11.119
But I do remember I had gotten, I kind of would would get these waves of heroic confidence, like the higher stakes it got, I would get like a little more like, I'm going to get this, you know, like it was my, this competitive street came out in me, and I would And sometimes say things that were like just a little like Hutzpahey in a way that was like risky, but I remember when Kobe, she threw an actual drink in my face.
但我确实记得我已经得到了，我会得到这些英雄般的自信，就像它得到的赌注越高，我会变得更像，我会得到这个，你知道，就像这是我的，这条竞争性的街道在我身上出现，有时我会以一种冒险的方式说一些有点像Hutzpahey的话，但我记得当科比时，她把一杯真正的饮料泼到我脸上。

00:57:11.119 --> 00:57:17.559
She had some water and she threw the water in my face and everyone laughed.
她拿了一些水，把水泼到我脸上，每个人都笑了。

00:57:17.559 --> 00:57:19.920
And I, this seems over at that point.
而我，似乎到那时就结束了。

00:57:19.920 --> 00:57:27.119
And I turned to the brass at CBS in 20th and I said, as if this process weren't humiliating enough.
20 日，我向哥伦比亚广播公司的高层求助，我说，好像这个过程还不够丢脸。

00:57:27.119 --> 00:57:31.191
And it got, you know, it got this like really big laugh.
你知道，它得到了很大的笑声。

00:57:31.191 --> 00:57:34.245
And I felt, um, I felt like that was good.
我觉得，嗯，我觉得那很好。

00:57:34.245 --> 00:57:46.244
You know, I just want them to know like, I just wanted that I, I, I, I always hated the power imbalance in being an actor and saying, like, please give me this role.
你知道，我只是想让他们知道，我只是想让我，我，我，我一直讨厌作为一名演员的权力不平衡，并说，就像，请给我这个角色。

00:57:46.244 --> 00:57:51.261
And I always wanted them to know like, I got something going on here.
我一直想让他们知道，我这里发生了一些事情。

00:57:51.261 --> 00:57:51.761
Yeah.
是的。

00:57:51.761 --> 00:57:53.361
I hope you understand.
我希望你能理解。

00:57:53.361 --> 00:58:01.505
So I just wanted to level it the tiniest bit because it's so, it's so outsized the power when you walk in there.
所以我只是想把它调平一点，因为当你走进那里时，它的力量是如此之大。

00:58:01.505 --> 00:58:04.996
And there are these executives that run empires.
还有这些管理帝国的高管。

00:58:04.860 --> 00:58:08.364
Seated in like bleacher level, like theater seating, like tiered seating.
坐在露天看台的位置，像剧院的座位，像分层的座位。

00:58:08.364 --> 00:58:10.860
Like it's a little fee, a little play just for them.
就像是一点费用，只为他们玩一点。

00:58:10.860 --> 00:58:13.260
The whole thing stage managed to make you nervous.
整个舞台让你紧张。

00:58:13.260 --> 00:58:14.318
It's not comfortable.
这不太舒服。

00:58:14.318 --> 00:58:15.327
It's very stressful.
压力很大。

00:58:15.327 --> 00:58:16.335
And it's on purpose.
这是故意的。

00:58:16.335 --> 00:58:22.940
They want to see that you can, you can rise to like be like really like under the gun and there's pressure in the air in that room.
他们希望看到你可以，你可以在枪口下表现得像真的一样，房间里的空气充满压力。

00:58:22.940 --> 00:58:25.563
And Carter and I, of course, feel like total frauds.
当然，卡特和我感觉自己完全是个骗子。

00:58:25.563 --> 00:58:28.541
We're sitting in these bleachers with all these executives.
我们和所有这些高管坐在看台上。

00:58:28.541 --> 00:58:33.284
Meanwhile, two months earlier, we're the people, you know, bringing our little script to them.
与此同时，两个月前，我们就是把我们的小剧本带给他们的人。

00:58:33.284 --> 00:58:36.110
Like, please, you know, we were the you a month earlier.
就像，拜托，你知道，我们是一个月前的你。

00:58:36.110 --> 00:58:37.876
And now we're in the judge e-seats.
现在我们坐在电子评委席上。

00:58:37.876 --> 00:58:42.014
And so like, I felt I had such empathy for you in that moment, but you were great.
就像，那一刻我觉得我对你很有同情心，但你很棒。

00:58:42.014 --> 00:58:44.688
And human Kobe, the energy of human Kobe, undeniable.
还有人类科比，人类科比的能量，不可否认。

00:58:44.688 --> 00:58:49.179
I did feel loved and supported by you guys, by Pam, by Rob Greenberg, by Megan and Dylan.
我确实感受到了你们、帕姆、罗布·格林伯格、梅根和迪伦的爱和支持。

00:58:49.179 --> 00:58:55.260
Like I felt like the people that I had established this rapport within that first room were really on my side.
我觉得在第一个房间里与我建立融洽关系的人真的站在我这边。

00:58:55.260 --> 00:58:58.739
So I felt really, I felt some wind at my sales.
所以我真的觉得我的销售有一些风。

00:58:58.739 --> 00:59:06.579
But I remember, I can't remember if we got the offer or it might have been a Friday, we maybe had to wait till a Monday.
但我记得，我不记得我们是否收到了offer，或者可能是周五，我们可能不得不等到周一。

00:59:06.579 --> 00:59:07.420
I can't remember.
我不记得了。

00:59:07.420 --> 00:59:11.219
I think it was, I don't think it was immediate but I got the job like within days.
我认为是的，我不认为这是立竿见影的，但我几天之内就得到了这份工作。

00:59:11.219 --> 00:59:17.340
Um, and then next year, you know, we're making a podcast about this.
嗯，明年，你知道，我们将制作一个关于此的播客。

00:59:17.340 --> 00:59:37.860
Do you guys know the West Memphis three, the, the, the three kids who were, um, railroaded into, they were on death row for killing this, um, I think girl, it was kind of a satanic panic thing.
你们知道西孟菲斯三人吗，这，这，三个孩子，嗯，被铁路关进死牢，因为杀死了这个，嗯，我想女孩，这是一种撒旦恐慌的事情。

00:59:37.860 --> 00:59:38.860
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

00:59:38.860 --> 00:59:42.739
And they were called the West Memphis three and they got put on death row as teenagers.
他们被称为西孟菲斯三人组，十几岁时就被关进死牢。

00:59:42.739 --> 00:59:45.036
they were, they were totally innocent.
他们是，他们是完全无辜的。

00:59:45.036 --> 00:59:46.789
It was like an absolute sham.
这绝对是一场骗局。

00:59:46.789 --> 00:59:50.053
But I think they were on death row for about 20 years.
但我认为他们在死囚牢房里待了大约20年。

00:59:50.053 --> 00:59:58.092
And there was this guy, Damian Eccles, who I ended up doing in the evening at Joe's pub with this kind of evening of written letters.
还有一个人，达米安·埃克尔斯（Damian Eccles），我晚上在乔的酒吧里和他一起写了这样的一封信。

00:59:58.092 --> 00:59:59.542
And I met him backstage.
我在后台遇见了他。

00:59:59.542 --> 01:00:01.960
And he'd been on death row for 20 years.
他在死囚牢房里已经呆了20年了。

01:00:01.960 --> 01:00:06.795
And I introduced myself to him because I had just seen a documentary about them.
我向他介绍了自己，因为我刚刚看了一部关于他们的纪录片。

01:00:06.795 --> 01:00:10.120
And, and, uh, he said, I, I hope it's okay to say this.
而且，呃，他说，我，我希望这样说可以。

01:00:10.120 --> 01:00:11.026
I'm such a fan.
我就是这样的粉丝。

01:00:11.026 --> 01:00:14.834
I watched so much how I met your mother when I was behind bars.
当我入狱时，我看了很多我是如何遇见你母亲的。

01:00:14.834 --> 01:00:15.438
Oh my God.
我的天啊。

01:00:15.438 --> 01:00:16.043
Oh my God.
我的天啊。

01:00:16.043 --> 01:00:17.917
I've never heard that from him.
我从来没有听他说过这样的话。

01:00:17.917 --> 01:00:21.543
And I said, can I ask you, like, what was it about the show?
我说，我能问你一下，这个节目是关于什么的吗？

01:00:21.543 --> 01:00:22.873
I'm always so curious.
我总是那么好奇。

01:00:22.873 --> 01:00:25.895
What was it about the show that you wanted to see?
您想看的节目是什么？

01:00:25.895 --> 01:00:36.109
And he said, he said, it was fake enough that it took me away from where I was, but it was real enough that it promised a world that I was hoping I could rejoin one day.
他说，他说，它足够假，它让我离开了原来的地方，但它又足够真实，它承诺了一个我希望有一天能重新加入的世界。

01:00:36.110 --> 01:00:36.610
Wow.
哇。

01:00:36.610 --> 01:00:37.110
Wow.
哇。

01:00:37.110 --> 01:00:37.610
Wow.
哇。

01:00:37.610 --> 01:00:38.514
That's amazing.
太棒了。

01:00:38.514 --> 01:00:45.932
And I just that always stayed with me that kind of like hyper real but real kind of quality and what that can do to people.
我只是一直伴随着我那种超真实但真实的品质以及它可以对人们做什么。

01:00:45.932 --> 01:00:55.159
You can look at the show as diversion from your troubles or you can look at the show as a meta commentary on your real troubles in your real life, right?
你可以把这个节目看作是你摆脱烦恼的消遣，或者你可以把这个节目看作是对你现实生活中真正麻烦的元评论，对吗？

01:00:55.159 --> 01:01:18.016
Like it's got this it's got this ability to meet people where they are that part of part of what we're doing Carter Craig and I keep talking about this mystery that we're trying to solve is like, why does how I met your mother, why is it lasted so long, why do new generations keep discovering it, and why does it seem to be medicine, like soul medicine for people in hard times?
就像它有这样的能力，它有能力与人们见面，这是我们正在做的事情的一部分，卡特·克雷格和我一直在谈论我们试图解决的这个谜团，就像是，为什么我是如何遇见你母亲的，为什么它持续了这么久，为什么新一代不断发现它，为什么它似乎是一种药物，就像人们在困难时期的灵魂药物一样？

01:01:18.016 --> 01:01:23.745
But you know, that story about Damian is like, I think really illustrates something about that.
